Your assessment at the previous step was: {
  "threat_level": "MEDIUM",
  "recommended_rung": 2,
  "recommended_action": "Rung 2, with operator approval, plus rungs 0 and 1. (1) Send base security to the pilot estimate on the base beach. Use the average of the five RF pilot fixes, about (-1815, -70), error 60 m. The individual fixes vary by up to about 60 m. Security should detain and question the pilot and have the drone landed (ROE-6.1). First confirm the beach is empty of bystanders (Z-BEACH). If security gets eyes on the drone, that gives PVID only if the report is current within 30 s and matches the track (ROE-2.4). (2) Rung 1: re-cue the gimbal S-GIM to the radar/WAC track, not the degraded acoustic position. It has found nothing on five cues to the acoustic fix. S-ACO is about 300 m from radar and is degraded (H-03). The drone is now turning right at about 65 deg per 20 s, so do not lead it in a straight line. Cue to the predicted orbit point, about (-1770, 480) at 08:21:40, or hold on the orbit centre about (-1655, 345). (3) Keep tracking with all sensors (rung 0). Confidence has dropped to LOW this step. S-RF is 245 m from radar and 234 m from WAC, which is over the 200 m limit in ROE-2.5. S-RF is operational, so nothing explains the gap. PID is not held until the RF fix and radar/WAC agree within 200 m again, or the gimbal sees the drone (ROE-2.3, ROE-3.4). S-RF altitude is also erratic (139, -72, 14, 101, 122 m against radar 55-69 m). Treat RF altitude and position as unreliable and watch for false telemetry. RF heading matches radar (345), which argues against spoofing. (4) Ask the tower whether any aircraft is using the approach corridor (N-12). T-1 is in Z-APPR. (5) No defeat option now. The pilot is reachable, the threat is MEDIUM, and ROE-1.5 says use the lowest rung that works. Raise the threat level if the drone heads for housing or other critical assets, if a payload is seen, or if the pilot is found to be off base or concealed."
}

